      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T18:44:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg, any thoughts on whether this makes sense?",
      "revId": "47572866a804fcbd67770a11fc1a3c849ed86f9d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f5c4366_88080a54",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T15:10:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess in general this seems fine. I certainly would want more details on exactly what the value returned by elapsedTime means.\n\nThe one general question I have, is this something that we think fits better on flush or submit? Are there different stats we might want on one vs the other? FWIW if we wanted something with submit I am adding a struct to submit calls here (currently in Ganesh) so it should be easier to add things, https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/907485",
      "parentUuid": "0ba52c81_602a3803",
      "revId": "47572866a804fcbd67770a11fc1a3c849ed86f9d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e10d9263_26016931",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 13150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T18:21:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027d be the result given by the underlying API\u0027s timer query mechanism: time elapsed in nanoseconds. We might have to sum this across multiple command buffers if multiple command buffers are used.\n\nI *think* it makes sense on the flush/recording level since that is when the command buffers are prepare AFAIK.",
      "parentUuid": "3f5c4366_88080a54",
      "revId": "47572866a804fcbd67770a11fc1a3c849ed86f9d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e98bb513_dc260997",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T18:38:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay yeah actually looking at the timer queries in Vulkan they are recorded in a command buffer. So doing them at Recorder insertion makes sense.\n\nSo to make sure we\u0027re all on the same page, we would add a query at the start of a command buffer and a query at the end. Then we\u0027ll calculate the difference and return that value as `elapsedTime` right?\n\nAt least for Graphite we would never be using multiple command buffers for a given Recording so I don\u0027t think we ever have to worry about summing things up. Ganesh on the other had may break a flush into multiple command buffers. However, since everything is still going to the same Queue, I believe it is still find to just have one start query in the first command buffer and one end query in the last command buffer. So no summing needed, but we would need logic to know that we\u0027re waiting on two different command buffers to have all our query data.",
      "parentUuid": "e10d9263_26016931",
      "revId": "47572866a804fcbd67770a11fc1a3c849ed86f9d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c4557cf_51ec2886",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 13150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T18:42:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, that\u0027s my thought for Graphite (compute the diff). In GL/Ganesh there is an actual elapsed version of the query, so no need to diff.\n\nI was only planning to do the impl for Dawn/Graphite and GL/Ganesh. So no real notion of command buffers in the Ganesh implementation. But, yeah, I think you\u0027re right if this were extended to other Ganesh backends.",
      "parentUuid": "e98bb513_dc260997",
      "revId": "47572866a804fcbd67770a11fc1a3c849ed86f9d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
